{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]There's a rabbit in the log and I ain't got my dog
How will I get him I [D7]know
[G]I'll get me a briar and twist it in his hair
[G]That way [D]I'll get him [G]I know
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]I know (yes I know) [G]I know (I surely know)
That's how I'll get him I [D7]know
[G]I'll get me a briar and twist it in his hair
[G]That way [D]I'll get him [G]I know
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I'll build me a fire and I'll cook that old hare
Roll him in the flames and make him brown
Have a feast here tonight while the moon is shining bright
And find me a place to lie down
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
To lie down (to lie down) to lie down (to lie down)
Find me a place to lie down
Have a feast here tonight while the moon is shining bright
And find me a place to lie down
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
I'm going down that track with my coat and my bag
Soles on my shoes are nearly gone
A little ways ahead there's a farmer's shed
That's where I'll rest my weary bones
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
Weary bones (weary bones) weary bones (your lazy bones)
That's where I'll rest my weary bones
A little way's ahead there's a farmer's shed
That's where I'll rest my weary bones
{end_of_verse}
